INSTALL - Gled build area
=========================

External software
-----------------

The base libsets need:

 ROOT      6, tested with 6.40         https://root.cern
           built with runtime_cxxmodules (the default on Linux)
 FLTK      1.3, with threads and GL    https://www.fltk.org
 GLEW
 DevIL     1.7                         https://openil.sourceforge.net
 freetype
 GSL

GledGTS needs GTS 0.7, Audio1 needs OpenAL, freealut and libvorbis. FTGL,
ROOT's fork of 2.1.2, is part of GledCore (Rnr/GL/FTGL.h and FTGL.cxx).
OpenSSL is used for authentication, but the RSA code still uses the
OpenSSL 1.x API, so use --nossl (below) with OpenSSL 3. A distribution's
packages cover everything (on Fedora: fltk-devel, glew-devel,
mesa-libGLU-devel, DevIL-devel, freetype-devel, gsl-devel, gts-devel,
openal-soft-devel, freealut-devel, libvorbis-devel); the gled-builder
repository can instead build them into one prefix.

Build procedure
---------------

1) Set up ROOT and point GLEDSYS at this directory, e.g. in (ba)sh:

     export ROOTSYS=<ROOT installation>
     export GLEDSYS=$PWD
     export PATH=$ROOTSYS/bin:$PATH

   configure takes GLEDSYS from the environment, so set it even if it is
   already set for another Gled tree.

2) Run ./configure with the options you need. Defaults are in
   configure.rc. Options can be given as --<opt>=<val> or -<opt> <val>,
   and their names can be abbreviated. The most relevant ones:

      -external      ':' separated list of directories to include and link
                     from; each <dir> implies -I<dir>/include and -L<dir>/lib
      -libsets       ':' separated list of libset names, or
                     <auto> for all libsets in -libsetpath,
                     <auto-prompt> to choose among them, or
                     <file:[filename]> for a file with one libset per line;
                     an entry <LibSet>=<dir> builds the libset in <dir>,
                     which must be named <LibSet>
      -libsetpath    ':' separated directories holding libset directories,
                     <dir>/<LibSet>/Makefile, relative to this directory;
                     default ../libsets
      -nossl         build without OpenSSL, so without authentication
      -debug         implies -DDEBUG and -g (otherwise -O)
      -ucpp <str>    user cpp-flags (e.g. -D_SOMETHING_)
      -ucxx <str>    user cxx-flags
      -uld  <str>    user ld-flags

   configure writes build_config, a perl dump of the configuration with
   the libsets in dependency order, Makefile.config, make/make_config.inc
   and build_env.sh, and runs make depend in each libset.

   configure --reconfigure [<libsets>] reuses the options in build_config;
   use it to add or remove libsets, or after editing build_config by hand.
   Changes of compiler flags or external directories need a full
   configure.

3) Set up the environment of this build and run make:

     source build_env.sh
     make -j8

   make builds all libraries and executables and links them into bin/ and
   lib/ here. It uses the default compiler; export CXX to use another.
   For each libset it first makes the dictionary, a C++ module, and then
   the libraries. A libset waits only for the libsets it requires, so with
   -j the others build in parallel.

   gled-create glass and gled-create stone write a new class and add it
   to the libset's glass.list or Stones/LinkDef.h, and make picks it up.
   Run ./configure --reconfigure before a method of any glass takes the
   new glass as an argument: project7 looks the glasses up in
   build_config.

Basing a build on existing builds
---------------------------------

To build a few libsets and reuse libsets that are already built
elsewhere, pass the other build directories with -base:

  ./configure -base <dir1>:<dir2> <other options>

A dependency that is not found in -libsetpath is looked up in those
builds by its manifest, <dir>/lib/<libset>.manifest, written when that
build was made. configure takes the libset ID, its directory, its
dependencies and its glasses from the manifest, compiles against the
headers in that directory and links the libset's bin, cfg, lib, macros and
perllib files into the local directory. Nothing in the base builds is run
or modified.

Libsets from other repositories
-------------------------------

Libsets kept in other repositories, such as gled-hep, are added with
-libsetpath ../libsets:<dir> or with -libsets <LibSet>=<dir>.
